-# Agent Note: Browser Target bridge and compact reconnect for the extension iframe
-
-Status: implemented
-
-English | [中文](2026-08-14-active-tab-dock.zh.md)
-
-## Problem
-
-The extension iframe needs Browser Target controls and a visible route to reconnect Harness without implying that an ambient Chrome tab is a Run binding. A loose iframe message or a page-content bridge would turn this UI into an untrusted control or context channel.
-
-## Decision
-
-`dsh-client-ui-browser-target` registers the Browser Target trigger in `conversation.input.left`, its picker in `conversation.input.overlay`, and an 18px `harness-reconnect` adapter in `sidebar.compact.action` only when the loopback iframe URL carries `dshBrowserTargetBridge=1`, a per-frame nonce, and the exact Chrome extension parent origin. The sidebar owns the small, deep list seam and places the adapter after the half-width workspace/session-plus-New-Session primary group and before compact Settings.
-
-Its apply-owned snapshot source accepts Browser Target snapshots only from `window.parent`, the exact extension origin, matching nonce, and a strictly increasing sequence. It sends target commands with the same requirements. The compact action sends `{ type: 'harness-reconnect/v1', nonce }` to that exact parent origin. The sidepanel first verifies the iframe `source`, loopback `origin`, and nonce, then invokes its existing `connect()` path. The payload remains limited to visible tab metadata and policy; reconnect neither transfers a Browser Target nor enters session/model context.
-
-## Alternatives considered
-
-- **Reuse Browser Target transfer** — would conflate a visible ambient tab or reconnect click with an explicitly bound Run target.
-- **Use DOM injection or a sidepanel overlay** — duplicates the Harness UI and sidesteps its mounted slot composition.
-- **Use wildcard `postMessage` origins** — loses the iframe-origin trust boundary.
-
-## Consequences
-
-Browser Target policy changes do not reconnect or migrate a Run; only the explicit compact action invokes the existing reconnect path. The UI intentionally remains absent in normal Web Harness deployments and may briefly remain empty until the first tab snapshot arrives. Focused extension and package tests pin the slot order, compact half-width and ellipsis rules, origin, nonce, sequence, opt-in, and reconnect message.
