-# Agent Note: Compact running-subagent entry
-
-Status: implemented
-
-English | [中文](2026-08-15-compact-running-subagent-entry.zh.md)
-
-## Problem
-
-At narrow widths, the conversation header is intentionally absent and the parent Session's subagent catalog no longer has a visible entry point while child work is still running.
-
-## Decision
-
-`ui-sidebar` declares `sidebar.compact.action`, rendered only by its compact presentation between New Session and Settings. `ui-subagent` occupies that seat with an icon and count only when the current Session's direct catalog has child rows whose catalog activity and live session summary both report running. Its hover, focus, and click menu uses those exact catalog addresses to open the existing child detail view, and shows only existing token and timing projections.
-
-Wide and rail presentations do not render the compact seat. The entry never derives state from another Session, and inactive, completed, failed, or otherwise non-running child rows remain absent.
-
-## Alternatives considered
-
-- **Keep the entry in the hidden conversation header** — the narrow shell does not render that header, so running work would remain undiscoverable.
-- **Show every historical child** — this would turn a live-work indicator into another full catalog and obscure the tasks that still need attention.
-- **Infer a child address from the session summary** — summaries lack the direct catalog mode required by `openSubagent`; the feature uses the existing catalog address instead.
-
-## Consequences
-
-The compact header gains a current-session-only path to active child transcripts without changing wide navigation. A newly selected parent can remain icon-free until its already-scheduled direct catalog refresh arrives, rather than guessing an address or polling a new data source. Component tests pin session isolation, running-state filtering, responsive shell placement, menu dismissal, and exact detail navigation.
