-# Agent Note: Harness-local Skill modes
-
-Status: implemented
-
-English | [中文](2026-08-15-harness-local-skill-modes.zh.md)
-
-## Problem
-
-Users need to stop or make manual individual Skills in Harness without editing a shared `SKILL.md` and unintentionally changing Claude Code or another agent.
-
-## Decision
-
-`dsh-skill-settings` stores a Host-wide `skill-settings.modes` map with `enabled`, `manual-only`, and `disabled` values. `SkillRegistry` owns the effective-policy projection for both summaries and loaded definitions, and intersects the local answer with authored frontmatter. `listSource()` is reserved for the authenticated Host settings view so a disabled entry remains manageable.
-
-The Web Skills page reads the active project's source catalog and effective controls, writes the existing settings namespace, and labels authored restrictions. The normal slash catalog continues to return only effective user-invocable entries.
-
-## Alternatives considered
-
-**Rewrite `SKILL.md`.** Rejected because the file is shared with other Skill consumers and a Harness choice must not change their behavior.
-
-**Hide entries only in the browser.** Rejected because direct model tool calls and user messages would still load the Skill.
-
-**Treat every Skill as a Loader plugin.** Rejected because Skills are discovered content, while the capability that changes is invocation policy.
-
-## Consequences
-
-- A disabled Skill is absent from model catalogs, rejected by the loader, and ignored by user `/name` injection.
-- Existing author restrictions remain stricter than a local enabled choice.
-- Modes apply across this Harness Host, while discovery continues to vary by session cwd and preset.
